01:16.601 --> 01:18.350
I hold it dearly in my heart and hope

01:20.041 --> 01:21.730
It'll come true someday soon

01:20.770 --> 01:20.810
- I'll Do Anything to Become a Librarian!
- I'll Do Anything to Become a Librarian!

01:20.980 --> 01:21.020
- I'll Do Anything to
- I'll Do Anything to

01:21.101 --> 01:21.140
- Ascendance of a Bookworm
- Ascendance of a Bookworm

01:25.106 --> 01:28.479
I don't have anything, nothing at all

01:28.480 --> 01:31.820
- But if I could have this one wish granted
- But if I could have this one wish granted

01:31.823 --> 01:34.510
It would fill the void inside my heart

01:39.160 --> 01:41.225
I can feel the warm breeze blowing

01:45.316 --> 01:47.339
And see shooting stars filling the sky

01:51.631 --> 01:51.670
They make me feel as if

01:53.681 --> 01:54.430
I can do anything, y'know?

01:59.246 --> 02:01.179
In this wonderful world

02:01.180 --> 02:02.725
Nothing is set in stone

02:05.770 --> 02:07.819
The as-yet untold future

02:07.820 --> 02:09.360
Shines brighter than the sun

02:12.801 --> 02:14.699
I want to take hold of my future

02:14.700 --> 02:16.180
With my own two hands

02:17.660 --> 02:20.119
And write pages filled with hope

02:23.370 --> 02:25.020
Into the book of my life

02:27.130 --> 02:29.630
Side Story: Chapter 1

02:29.631 --> 02:32.130
Justus' Flawless Plan for Infiltrating
the Lower City

02:34.680 --> 02:36.640
<i>My name is Justus.</i>

02:37.260 --> 02:39.139
<i>On Master Ferdinand's command,</i>

02:39.140 --> 02:41.640
<i>we, as his close aides,
are infiltrating the lower city.</i>

02:41.890 --> 02:43.640
<i>It's the beginning of summer.</i>

02:44.310 --> 02:46.150
So this is the lower city...

02:51.030 --> 02:53.359
I'm shocked you can deal with this, Justus.

02:53.360 --> 02:55.609
Are you not bothered by the smell?

02:55.610 --> 02:57.449
I don't really have a choice in the matter.

02:57.450 --> 03:01.449
Our first priority should be locating
a store that sells commoner's clothes.

03:01.450 --> 03:02.500
What's that?

03:02.500 --> 03:04.040
What are nobles doing here?

03:02.501 --> 03:05.830
It seems we weren't careful
enough with our choice of clothing.

03:08.000 --> 03:09.460
Thank you.

03:09.920 --> 03:11.249
Oh, actually...

03:11.250 --> 03:12.799
Have you heard of the Myne Workshop?

03:12.800 --> 03:14.000
It produces plant-based paper.

03:14.220 --> 03:15.630
Myne Workshop?

03:16.930 --> 03:19.469
I'm sorry. I haven't heard of it.

03:19.470 --> 03:21.220
I see.

03:26.890 --> 03:28.399
These clothes smell awful too!

03:28.400 --> 03:31.649
They'll require washing magic
to even be considered wearable.

03:31.650 --> 03:32.940
Stop complaining.

03:33.280 --> 03:35.109
Let's get on with the investigation.

03:35.110 --> 03:36.949
You saw the reaction at
the secondhand clothes shop.

03:36.950 --> 03:39.819
People here are suspicious
of unfamiliar faces.

03:39.820 --> 03:41.869
The commoners are cautious,

03:41.870 --> 03:43.449
and have a very tight-knit community.

03:43.450 --> 03:45.829
I'm getting a headache from the stench.

03:45.830 --> 03:49.460
This mission is way worse
than gathering materials.

03:55.300 --> 03:58.430
I won't be able to make
any progress if you're with me.

03:58.800 --> 04:02.430
<i>I walked my incapacitated
partner to an inn,</i>

04:02.850 --> 04:05.930
<i>and headed to the Gilberta
Company to investigate further.</i>

04:06.230 --> 04:08.440
Mark, please walk Myne home.

04:08.640 --> 04:09.939
That won't be necessary.

04:09.940 --> 04:12.819
I'm meeting up with my mom at the
central plaza today to do some shopping,

04:12.820 --> 04:14.690
and we'll go home together afterwards.

04:21.320 --> 04:23.410
<i>Is this the place?</i>

04:23.660 --> 04:26.789
<i>I heard it's the main trading
partner of the Myne Workshop,</i>

04:26.790 --> 04:28.920
<i>but it seems to be some
kind of clothing shop.</i>

04:29.330 --> 04:32.050
<i>Why would they trade with a workshop
that makes "plant-based paper"?</i>

04:33.500 --> 04:37.050
<i>Oh, those are some
intriguing hair accessories.</i>

04:40.220 --> 04:43.850
I'm terribly sorry,
but do you need anything at our shop?

04:45.260 --> 04:49.850
Ah, no, it's just that I spotted
some interesting hair accessories...

04:50.690 --> 04:52.310
I don't really need anything.

04:56.190 --> 04:59.699
And so you came back here
without asking any questions?

04:59.700 --> 05:04.700
Yeah. They're so cautious that I won't be able to
investigate further without arousing suspicion.

05:05.240 --> 05:06.450
Which is why...

05:08.040 --> 05:12.119
According to the report, Myne's
residence is close to the south gate.

05:12.120 --> 05:15.550
I will locate it and gather
information in the area.

05:15.840 --> 05:18.459
You never fail to impress.

05:18.460 --> 05:20.980
Even under close inspection,
you look like a simple farmer now.

05:21.630 --> 05:23.550
I'm sorry for being so useless.

05:23.800 --> 05:25.849
I'll be goin' now.

05:25.850 --> 05:29.560
Try 'n' get used to it a lil'
bit by the end of th' day.

05:35.440 --> 05:40.030
<i>I had studied my surroundings and
crafted an innocuous disguise; a farmer.</i>

05:44.240 --> 05:46.449
Oh, so sorry!

05:46.450 --> 05:47.489
Ya okay?

05:47.490 --> 05:49.330
Yeah...

05:52.250 --> 05:55.919
Actually, what kind of business
does a farmer have here?

05:55.920 --> 05:57.669
There's no market around here.

05:57.670 --> 06:00.299
I'm not anyone suspicious!

06:00.300 --> 06:01.969
I've somethin' to do 'ere, ya see.

06:01.970 --> 06:03.930
Ya know a girl called Myne?

06:04.430 --> 06:05.390
Myne?!

06:05.391 --> 06:08.759
Yeah. She really helped me out, ya see.

06:08.760 --> 06:11.639
I'm lookin' for 'er to thank 'er for it.

06:11.640 --> 06:13.139
I don't know her, no...

06:13.140 --> 06:17.650
I hear she makes plant-based
paper in th' Myne Workshop...

06:18.400 --> 06:20.279
I'm telling you I don't know her!

06:20.280 --> 06:21.819
Outsiders shouldn't wander around too much.

06:21.820 --> 06:24.280
Don't come crying to me
if people mistake you for a thief!

06:24.570 --> 06:26.700
Now go back to where you came from!

06:27.280 --> 06:29.580
I won't let you off the
hook if I see you here again!

06:32.080 --> 06:34.249
I guess that's that.

06:34.250 --> 06:36.580
I'll just ask around here instead.

06:45.840 --> 06:47.850
We gathered so much today!

06:48.260 --> 06:50.929
Those children are around
the same age as Myne...

06:50.930 --> 06:52.060
Perfect.

06:53.600 --> 06:55.480
Hey, ya there!

06:54.020 --> 06:55.480
But you know...

06:56.560 --> 06:58.610
D'ya know a girl called Myne?

06:58.810 --> 07:00.109
Myne?!

07:00.110 --> 07:02.360
I-I have nothing to do with her, I swear!

07:04.450 --> 07:07.659
Are you still scared of her?

07:07.660 --> 07:08.660
Scared?

07:08.990 --> 07:13.579
Yeah, she chewed him out
for breaking something of hers...

07:13.580 --> 07:14.580
Right?

07:16.330 --> 07:19.750
She was really nice to me, though.

07:20.000 --> 07:23.209
Are you sure that was Myne and not Tuuli?

07:23.210 --> 07:26.509
Yeah. Myne would never be kind to others.

07:26.510 --> 07:27.510
Tuuli?

07:27.800 --> 07:29.759
Myne's sister.

07:29.760 --> 07:31.890
Hey, Tuuli!

07:32.220 --> 07:33.390
What is it?

07:33.850 --> 07:36.979
Gramps here says he's looking for Myne.

07:36.980 --> 07:38.020
For Myne?

07:38.230 --> 07:41.979
Yeah, I want to thank
'er for helpin' me out.

07:41.980 --> 07:44.530
An' give 'er some of
these vegetables I grew.

07:44.740 --> 07:47.530
Are you sure it was Myne?

07:47.740 --> 07:50.530
I'm pretty sure that was 'er name...

07:50.740 --> 07:52.990
Was she with someone?

07:53.200 --> 07:56.250
Huh? No, I think she was alone...

07:56.460 --> 07:58.709
Then it couldn't have been her.

07:58.710 --> 08:00.750
Myne can't walk around on her own.

08:00.960 --> 08:02.750
She can't?

08:03.000 --> 08:07.130
Yeah. She's quite frail, so she has to be
escorted by someone whenever she goes out.

08:07.380 --> 08:10.140
I see. I can't believe I
got the wrong person...

08:10.340 --> 08:13.640
D'you know about th'
Myne Workshop, maybe, then?

08:13.890 --> 08:15.099
Not really, no...

08:15.100 --> 08:16.520
I don't!

08:17.060 --> 08:19.150
I-It's fine if ya don't, I guess.

08:19.520 --> 08:21.689
Sorry for holdin' ya up.

08:21.690 --> 08:23.980
Please take this as an apology!

08:25.530 --> 08:26.740
See ya around!

08:30.490 --> 08:34.120
<i>It seems I'm not having
much luck this time...</i>

08:43.590 --> 08:46.340
She's so weak that she needs
someone escorting her, huh?

08:46.590 --> 08:50.840
I didn't think there would be such
a lack of information in her neighborhood.

08:51.260 --> 08:52.800
What are you planning to do?

08:53.100 --> 08:56.309
I'll infiltrate the Merchant's Guild
at night and search for clues.

08:56.310 --> 08:59.309
We'll make no progress otherwise.

08:59.310 --> 09:01.939
Additionally, Myne's father
is a guard at the south gate.

09:01.940 --> 09:03.400
Let's tail him.

09:05.150 --> 09:07.900
Thank the gods for night duty!

09:12.280 --> 09:15.160
I see, so you'll be a father too now!

09:15.620 --> 09:18.789
How did you decide on
the names for your children?

09:18.790 --> 09:20.250
Names?

09:20.460 --> 09:23.789
Yeah. I talk about it
with Corinna every night,

09:23.790 --> 09:25.250
but we can't decide on anything.

09:25.540 --> 09:29.009
Come on, the child isn't due until winter.

09:29.010 --> 09:30.330
You're getting ahead of yourself.

09:36.760 --> 09:38.520
Are you okay now?

09:41.020 --> 09:43.849
It's worse in here than outside.

09:43.850 --> 09:46.020
Can't we move onto the next plan?

09:46.440 --> 09:48.400
Okay. Let's go.

10:02.620 --> 10:08.709
<i>The next day, we went to places that trade
with the Gilberta Company to ask questions.</i>

10:08.710 --> 10:09.760
Myne?

10:10.130 --> 10:12.009
That little girl, right?

10:12.010 --> 10:14.389
She writes up supply orders
by herself with no issue.

10:14.390 --> 10:15.760
She's really something!

10:16.180 --> 10:17.760
Yes, I know her.

10:18.060 --> 10:20.599
She could put most adults to shame
with how she handles business.

10:20.600 --> 10:22.390
No issues with payment either.

10:22.770 --> 10:25.729
<i>Everyone calls her an odd child,</i>

10:25.730 --> 10:29.650
<i>but to me it seems more
like she's simply exceptional.</i>

10:30.360 --> 10:33.649
<i>In any case, she seems
to handle her work well,</i>

10:33.650 --> 10:36.810
<i>so there shouldn't be any problems making
her an apprentice blue shrine maiden.</i>

10:37.370 --> 10:40.040
<i>We'll report the details upon our return.</i>

10:40.450 --> 10:41.450
That is all.

10:43.910 --> 10:47.170
Since we're already here,
shall we take a look at the market?

10:47.330 --> 10:48.919
We're done with our task.

10:48.920 --> 10:49.920
Let's hurry back...

10:50.340 --> 10:51.880
Just for a bit.

11:01.930 --> 11:04.890
Sir, where did you get this book?

11:05.100 --> 11:07.900
A noble pawned it off.

11:08.310 --> 11:09.400
A noble?

11:10.070 --> 11:11.730
Could I see it?

11:12.030 --> 11:15.609
Of course! Look at it as much as you want!

11:15.610 --> 11:18.569
The only person who ever
took interest in that book,

11:18.570 --> 11:21.660
not counting you, was a weird child.

11:22.240 --> 11:23.620
A weird child?

11:23.870 --> 11:27.919
Yeah! She suddenly dropped to the ground...

11:27.920 --> 11:31.379
I understand that I cannot buy it,
but at least let me touch it!

11:31.380 --> 11:33.760
I want to at least enjoy
the sweet fragrance of ink.

11:34.050 --> 11:35.760
Please, I beg you.

11:36.760 --> 11:38.510
I see.

11:39.970 --> 11:42.770
Could I buy it for this much?

11:47.020 --> 11:51.069
<i>She showed interest in books and
wanted to enjoy the fragrance of ink.</i>

11:51.070 --> 11:52.230
<i>She's indeed quite odd.</i>

11:53.150 --> 11:58.200
<i>Now I actually want to see
for myself what kind of girl she is.</i>

12:01.700 --> 12:03.450
Next Chapter

12:03.451 --> 12:05.200
A Visit to Lady Corinna's House

12:05.620 --> 12:09.829
Lord Ferdinand, the
situation is blah-blah blah-blah.

12:09.830 --> 12:10.879
I see.

12:10.880 --> 12:13.249
Come to think of it,

12:13.250 --> 12:15.919
the first time I saw her, she was savoring
the fragrance of ink in the sacred book.

12:15.920 --> 12:18.089
In front of you as well, Lord Ferdinand?!

12:18.090 --> 12:21.509
She's truly an intriguing child!

12:21.510 --> 12:23.889
What kind of child is she?

12:23.890 --> 12:25.559
She sets my heart aflutter!

12:25.560 --> 12:27.890
I want to meet her! Talk to her!

12:28.480 --> 12:30.979
You're both weird, so
you might get along well.

12:30.980 --> 12:32.559
That aside, let's see.

12:32.560 --> 12:35.110
What kind of person is she?

12:35.730 --> 12:37.715
Ascendance of

12:35.730 --> 12:37.715
I'll Do Anything to Become

12:37.716 --> 12:39.700
a Bookworm

12:37.716 --> 12:39.700
a Librarian!

12:42.320 --> 12:45.540
<i>While Justus was gathering
information about Myne,</i>

12:45.910 --> 12:48.870
<i>Myne received a summons from Corinna.</i>

12:52.750 --> 12:54.500
A summons?!

12:54.840 --> 12:57.510
What have you done, Myne?

13:05.760 --> 13:08.265
Side Story: Chapter 2

13:08.266 --> 13:10.770
A Visit to Lady Corinna's House

13:11.020 --> 13:15.770
Mrs. Corinna said she wants to see
my baptism dress and hair ornament.

13:16.030 --> 13:17.280
Can I show them to her?

13:19.610 --> 13:22.780
I don't think Lady Corinna
would be interested in seeing that.

13:23.490 --> 13:25.030
I see...

13:26.290 --> 13:28.200
I'll decline the summons then.

13:28.410 --> 13:29.960
You can't decline!

13:30.160 --> 13:32.540
What should I do then?

13:34.630 --> 13:36.670
Uh...

13:40.340 --> 13:41.340
Gods!

13:42.260 --> 13:44.470
I can't give you an answer so suddenly.

13:44.640 --> 13:47.309
Mom seems unusually troubled.

13:47.310 --> 13:48.599
Yeah.

13:48.600 --> 13:53.309
Myne, are you going to take the dress
and hair ornament to her house to show her?

13:53.310 --> 13:55.399
Yeah, I think that's what I'll have to do.

13:55.400 --> 13:58.149
Can I come with you?

13:58.150 --> 13:59.780
I'll ask.

14:01.200 --> 14:02.740
I love you, Myne!

14:02.990 --> 14:06.490
Wait a moment. I haven't
said we're going yet.

14:06.660 --> 14:08.829
But we wouldn't decline, would we?

14:08.830 --> 14:09.870
We can't, right?

14:12.750 --> 14:13.870
What are you gonna do?

14:14.460 --> 14:15.710
But...

14:18.000 --> 14:20.130
What ever shall we do?

14:23.300 --> 14:25.390
I wonder how I should greet her.

14:25.590 --> 14:28.849
"It's nice to meet you.
Thank you for your invitation."

14:28.850 --> 14:29.850
How's that?

14:29.930 --> 14:31.639
What about me, Myne?

14:31.640 --> 14:35.650
You should just smile and say
"I've been looking forward to it," Tuuli.

14:35.940 --> 14:39.150
It's nice to meet you.
Thank you for your invitation.

14:39.400 --> 14:41.320
I've been looking forward to it!

14:42.360 --> 14:43.900
Yeah, good!

14:44.110 --> 14:47.409
It's nice to meet you.
Thank you for your invitation.

14:47.410 --> 14:49.540
I've been looking forward to it!

14:50.410 --> 14:53.789
It's nice to meet you.
Thank you for your invitation.

14:53.790 --> 14:55.750
I've been looking forward to it!

14:58.290 --> 15:00.420
Mrs. Corinna! Hello!

15:01.550 --> 15:03.299
Welcome, Myne.

15:03.300 --> 15:06.429
It's nice to see you, Myne's
mother, Myne's sister.

15:06.430 --> 15:07.929
I'm Corinna.

15:07.930 --> 15:09.680
Good afternoon, Mrs. Corinna!

15:10.140 --> 15:11.680
Please come on in.

15:11.930 --> 15:13.850
Thank you! It was very
kind of you to invite us.

15:18.480 --> 15:21.070
<i>They're way too nervous.</i>

15:28.490 --> 15:29.830
Thank you for having us.

15:30.080 --> 15:32.079
It is nice to meet you, Lady Corinna.

15:32.080 --> 15:34.329
I am Myne's mother, Effa.

15:34.330 --> 15:36.830
Thank you so much for your invitation.

15:37.040 --> 15:39.749
Lady Corinna, I'm Tuuli.

15:39.750 --> 15:41.919
I've been looking forward to this.

15:41.920 --> 15:43.920
I'm so glad I got to meet you.

15:45.380 --> 15:47.679
I've been looking forward to it as well.

15:47.680 --> 15:49.849
Please wait here a moment.

15:49.850 --> 15:52.100
I'll have some tea prepared.

15:52.810 --> 15:56.350
I really wanted to see Myne's dress.

15:56.640 --> 15:59.350
Thank you for taking
the time to come visit me.

16:02.150 --> 16:04.070
It's so sweet!

16:05.610 --> 16:07.110
It's beautiful!

16:07.450 --> 16:11.120
I adjusted Tuuli's old dress.

16:11.450 --> 16:14.370
I'm surprised to see such adjustments.

16:14.830 --> 16:17.789
It is easier than sewing
something from scratch.

16:17.790 --> 16:21.419
We took the parts that were too big
or too long and pinned them up,

16:21.420 --> 16:23.839
and added a few ruffles here and there.

16:23.840 --> 16:25.010
I mean, Mom did!

16:25.590 --> 16:28.510
Can I ask you a few questions?

16:28.720 --> 16:31.760
Of course, I will do my
best to answer them.

16:33.970 --> 16:36.140
This is the hair ornament.

16:36.350 --> 16:39.139
I've never seen anything like this before.

16:39.140 --> 16:42.150
I made the big white flower.

16:42.360 --> 16:46.280
I see! You did a really good job, Tuuli.

16:46.780 --> 16:48.400
Thank you!

16:48.780 --> 16:53.909
I'd like to order some of these
to be made at my workshop,

16:53.910 --> 16:54.910
is that fine?

16:55.120 --> 16:56.199
Of course!

16:56.200 --> 16:57.789
It depends on the offer.

16:57.790 --> 17:00.540
M-M-Myne!

17:00.750 --> 17:04.629
Hair ornaments are an important
source of income during winter.

17:04.630 --> 17:06.550
I can't agree to this just like that.

17:06.710 --> 17:08.759
If you really want to make them,

17:08.760 --> 17:10.549
I'd like you to buy the right to do that.

17:10.550 --> 17:12.550
Otherwise it'll be a problem for us.

17:13.220 --> 17:14.220
Myne...

17:14.430 --> 17:15.679
Myne...

17:15.680 --> 17:17.519
I'm sorry, Lady Corinna.

17:17.520 --> 17:19.389
Please stay quiet, Mom.

17:19.390 --> 17:21.520
This is important.

17:21.900 --> 17:23.270
Myne...

17:23.520 --> 17:25.439
It's fine.

17:25.440 --> 17:29.530
Please talk to Benno about this, Myne.

17:29.900 --> 17:31.530
I will.

17:32.820 --> 17:34.280
It's nice to meet you.

17:34.620 --> 17:36.539
I'm Corinna's brother, Benno.

17:36.540 --> 17:38.499
It's nice to meet you, Lord Benno.

17:38.500 --> 17:40.289
I'm Myne's mother, Effa.

17:40.290 --> 17:42.499
Thank you for taking
good care of my daughter.

17:42.500 --> 17:44.749
I'm Tuuli, Mr. Benno, sir.

17:44.750 --> 17:47.050
It's a pleasure to meet you.

17:48.130 --> 17:50.050
What do you need, Corinna?

17:50.380 --> 17:51.549
Actually...

17:51.550 --> 17:56.719
Mrs. Corinna wants to buy exclusive
rights to sell the hair ornaments.

17:56.720 --> 17:59.680
How much will you buy it for, Mr. Benno?

18:04.270 --> 18:05.439
You're joking.

18:05.440 --> 18:06.940
I'm negotiating.

18:10.610 --> 18:11.820
How's that?!

18:13.160 --> 18:15.989
I can't sell it for such a small amount.

18:15.990 --> 18:18.540
It might be better to sell
it to Frieda in that case.

18:18.870 --> 18:23.540
Hey! Isn't Lutz supposed to be selling
whatever is made in the Myne Workshop?!

18:25.830 --> 18:29.379
Whatever is made in the Myne Workshop, yes.

18:29.380 --> 18:31.300
Instructions are not
included in that agreement.

18:31.510 --> 18:33.509
You little! What kind of logic is that?!

18:33.510 --> 18:35.429
Threatening me won't achieve anything.

18:35.430 --> 18:38.760
That just doesn't work on me, Mr. Benno.

18:44.020 --> 18:45.770
Myne's amazing.

18:46.440 --> 18:50.360
Tuuli, Effa, this might take
a while, so come with me.

18:52.240 --> 18:54.279
Myne really is amazing.

18:54.280 --> 18:57.530
Being able to talk
business with my brother!

18:57.780 --> 19:00.489
I've never seen Myne like that.

19:00.490 --> 19:04.659
She gets feverish easily,
and can't help with much at home,

19:04.660 --> 19:07.209
so I'd never imagined she could
argue like that with adults...

19:07.210 --> 19:09.800
That's a side of her I've never seen.

19:11.090 --> 19:13.919
Let's just leave the
business talk to those two,

19:13.920 --> 19:16.800
and have a talk about needlework ourselves.

19:17.340 --> 19:18.340
Sure!

19:18.510 --> 19:20.009
So pretty...

19:20.010 --> 19:22.810
How do you make such wonderful clothes?

19:23.270 --> 19:26.060
Could you show me, Lady Corinna?

19:26.520 --> 19:28.559
The technique is indeed important,

19:28.560 --> 19:31.820
but it's also very important
to see a lot of things for yourself.

19:32.360 --> 19:34.070
Look at this, for example.

19:35.740 --> 19:37.909
The shape of the flowers in this embroidery

19:37.910 --> 19:41.280
is something based on
flowers I picked in the forest.

19:43.870 --> 19:46.539
If you make a habit of carefully
observing your surroundings,

19:46.540 --> 19:49.040
it will come in handy
when designing things.

19:49.540 --> 19:50.840
I see...

19:52.170 --> 19:54.629
I want to become an apprentice seamstress

19:54.630 --> 19:58.800
so that I can one day make beautiful clothes
like the ones you make, Lady Corinna!

19:59.010 --> 20:02.180
I see. Good luck, Tuuli!

20:02.560 --> 20:03.930
Thank you!

20:04.810 --> 20:07.140
And you used to be such an innocent child!

20:07.600 --> 20:11.230
That's also one of the results
of your teachings, Mr. Benno.

20:17.990 --> 20:20.030
The deal is made.

20:21.240 --> 20:23.790
Seems like they're done.

20:24.080 --> 20:27.829
Mom! Could you show Mrs. Corinna
how to make the hair ornament?

20:27.830 --> 20:28.830
I will.

20:30.790 --> 20:32.209
I'm tired.

20:32.210 --> 20:33.749
Good job.

20:33.750 --> 20:36.970
How much did you settle on in the end?

20:37.420 --> 20:40.840
I'll base my prices for
the hair ornaments on that.

20:46.480 --> 20:49.560
I'm impressed you got
that much out of my brother!

20:50.770 --> 20:55.480
Your workshop has the exclusive right to sell the
hair ornaments for the next year, Mrs. Corinna.

20:55.980 --> 20:58.240
How much was it, Myne?

21:01.530 --> 21:03.490
Is it so much you can't tell me?

21:04.080 --> 21:05.829
It was a reasonable price,

21:05.830 --> 21:08.250
so I could tell you, but I'd rather not.

21:08.660 --> 21:10.120
Tell me, Myne!

21:11.960 --> 21:13.460
Tell me, Myne!

21:15.750 --> 21:17.590
Tell me, Myne!

21:19.260 --> 21:22.590
One large gold and seven small golds.

21:26.180 --> 21:27.679
Wait a second.

21:27.680 --> 21:29.480
Did you say "gold"?!

21:29.680 --> 21:31.809
It sounds like a lot of money,

21:31.810 --> 21:35.729
but it's a reasonable price
for the transfer of rights!

21:35.730 --> 21:37.649
I'm not Mr. Benno,

21:37.650 --> 21:40.110
I don't go around overcharging people!

21:42.160 --> 21:44.620
You did well, Myne.

21:45.160 --> 21:46.080
Thank you!

21:46.081 --> 21:49.960
It seems you'll be able to celebrate
your child's birth in peace!

21:55.920 --> 22:00.090
<i>And just like that, our visit to Mrs.
Corinna's house concluded without incident.</i>

22:05.510 --> 22:07.870
Tell me, oh my angel

22:07.871 --> 22:10.229
tell me, oh my angel

22:10.230 --> 22:14.710
oh my lovely, let me dream again

22:14.711 --> 22:19.190
oh my lovely, let me dream again

22:19.690 --> 22:20.900
I gently brush my hair

22:20.901 --> 22:22.110
I gently brush my hair

22:23.490 --> 22:26.120
- And put a hairpin through it
- And put a hairpin through it

22:26.123 --> 22:27.910
- In the sea of green
- In the sea of green

22:27.913 --> 22:29.515
A flower ornament blooms

22:29.516 --> 22:31.119
A flower ornament blooms

22:31.120 --> 22:33.370
- It is a gift from my angel
- It is a gift from my angel

22:34.710 --> 22:35.980
It touches my forehead

22:35.981 --> 22:37.250
It touches my forehead

22:38.630 --> 22:39.945
Oh so gently

22:39.946 --> 22:41.259
Oh so gently

22:41.260 --> 22:43.130
- And it reminds me
- And it reminds me

22:43.133 --> 22:44.695
Of the warm light that gathered

22:44.696 --> 22:46.259
Of the warm light that gathered

22:46.260 --> 22:48.510
- To bring my angel into this world
- To bring my angel into this world

22:49.310 --> 22:50.935
This fever is making me delirious

22:50.936 --> 22:52.560
This fever is making me delirious

22:53.140 --> 22:55.330
Ah, these times are so dear to me

22:55.331 --> 22:57.519
Ah, these times are so dear to me

22:57.520 --> 22:59.400
There must have been something more

22:59.401 --> 23:01.279
There must have been something more

23:01.280 --> 23:03.155
Some greater force that led me to you

23:03.156 --> 23:05.029
Some greater force that led me to you

23:05.030 --> 23:07.535
Our fates tangle and
unravel as we become family

23:07.536 --> 23:10.040
Our fates tangle and
unravel as we become family

23:16.460 --> 23:17.815
I have been always living

23:17.816 --> 23:19.170
I have been always living

23:20.670 --> 23:22.460
- Inside a book
- Inside a book

23:24.420 --> 23:25.965
But then my heart melted

23:25.966 --> 23:27.509
But then my heart melted

23:27.510 --> 23:29.785
And now I have experienced

23:29.786 --> 23:32.060
And now I have experienced

23:32.930 --> 23:34.270
- The real world
- The real world

23:34.273 --> 23:36.085
Back to the main story

23:36.086 --> 23:37.900
Back to the main story

23:38.100 --> 23:42.399
High Priest, I want to see
side stories of more people!

23:42.400 --> 23:45.239
I'm hoping for that as well.

23:45.240 --> 23:47.160
We just have to pray to the gods.

23:47.700 --> 23:48.739
Pray?

23:48.740 --> 23:51.990
I don't know what gods merchants pray to,

23:52.540 --> 23:57.829
but O Goddess of Time, Dregarnuhr,
let your threads weave together once more!

23:57.830 --> 23:59.499
Praise be to the gods.

23:59.500 --> 24:01.629
Praise be to the gods.

24:01.630 --> 24:03.960
Praise be to the gods!
